# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
# Used only while the image is built (live-build removes it afterwards, so
# users can still install any of these). The image installs Recommends, as
# Debian does by default; these packages must not come in that way: servers
# that would listen on the network or run in the background on every
# Zovelis OS system. (If a package ever *depends* on one of them, the build
# stops, which is the point.)

Explanation: mail servers (pulled in through "default-mta" recommendations)
Package: exim4-daemon-light exim4-daemon-heavy postfix sendmail-bin opensmtpd
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1

Explanation: remote login and RPC services
Package: openssh-server telnetd rpcbind
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1

Explanation: legacy CUPS printer browsing (UDP port 631); driverless
Explanation: printing works through avahi and cups itself
Package: cups-browsed
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1

Explanation: background services the desktop does not use (KDE PIM's
Explanation: database server, phone pairing daemon), KDE's own welcome
Explanation: wizard (the Zovelis Welcome app replaces it) and Debian's
Explanation: package-usage reporting
Package: akonadi-server kdeconnect plasma-welcome popularity-contest
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1
